WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:15.220
(Casting)

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.760
Betrayal cuts deep.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.360
Losing hurts, especially when you lose on the biggest stage your game has to offer,

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:28.360
when you lose in front of everyone, when you lose to the underdogs.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.720
But there’s something worse than losing.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.400
There’s nothing more painful than being betrayed.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.640
Seeing someone you considered a friend turn against you, turn against the philosophy you

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:45.540
once shared, turn against the band of brothers you put together to win with.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.720
And there’s nothing better than getting revenge.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:01:08.960
(Casting)

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.340
OG was founded on a simple principle.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:18.820
Johan “Big Dady N0tail” Sundestein and Tal “Fly” Aizik were tired of being tossed

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:22.440
from team to team without really getting a chance to develop.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.380
They believed that if a team stuck together for long enough,

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:28.140
If they believed in their ability to play together.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.120
They could win anything.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:37.800
(Casting)

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.260
They were almost right.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:42.260
(Casting)

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:48.119
OG won four Dota 2 Majors, more than any other team in history, and every time The International

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.100
came around, they were favorites.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.340
"Prediction one way or the other."

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.040
"OG."

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.600
With Fly at the helm as captain and N0tail at his side, OG looked strong going

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:58.600
into TI.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:04.360
They boasted team chemistry, one of the best players in Dota history and promising rookies.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.220
But they never succeeded.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.680
Things shifted ahead of TI8.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:17.280
The OG of the 2017-2018 season was not the OG fans came to recognize.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.620
The team just couldn’t put together wins when it mattered, falling to weaker teams

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.400
and lagging behind in the Dota 2 Pro Circuit.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.020
It looked like they weren’t going to make it to TI.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:31.660
In May, Fly broke the promise on which OG was founded.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:36.620
After two years of leading, building and supporting OG, he left.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:42.640
He took Gustav “S4” Magnusson and went to Evil Geniuses, long considered North America’s

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.640
best team.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:47.800
Evil Geniuses has never had the player loyalty that defined OG.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:52.380
That isn’t necessarily a bad thing, as the team is a perennial TI powerhouse.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.320
(Casting)

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:01.440
But it means that even after winning TI, they were willing to drop one of the players

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.840
that earned them the Aegis.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:21.800
They’ve got the money, the reputation and the core talent that could convince any player

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.350
to leave one team and join their hallowed
ranks.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:26.820
And Fly was convinced.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.520
"Fly and S4, why did you leave OG."

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:35.040
"The team hasn't worked for a long time, and I can say personally that I lost a lot of motivation

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:41.800
when the whole situation arised where I could join EG. I felt a new surge of motivation.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.380
Where I felt this is really a team I could win with.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.800
As opposed to the previous team where I felt we kinda hit a dead end.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.560
And yeah I want to win and I want to do it with teammates I believe in."

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:55.880
The change meant that both EG and OG would have to go through the open qualifiers to

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:02.200
make TI, but the addition of Fly and S4 made EG suddenly look like serious contenders to

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.820
lift the Aegis of champions, at least on paper.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:09.100
OG on the other hand were disregarded.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.940
Without their captain and one of their star players, fans didn’t even think they could

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.260
make it through the open qualifiers.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:20.840
OG signed Topias “Topson” Taavitsainen, a promising young rookie, and moved their

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:24.880
coach, Sebastien “Ceb” Debs onto the main lineup.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:30.500
Still, few had OG pegged to make a deep run at TI, or even make it at all.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:35.600
But if there’s anything that can fuel a team to victory, it’s revenge.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:44.160
(Casting)

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.440
But even once they made it to TI, hopes weren’t high for OG.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:54.680
"There's still a lot of questions around OG though, cause you look at LGD are tagged up in the top three

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:01.960
to go through. But OG were a team that came through — they obviously had their roster ripped apart by

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:03.080
Evil Geniuses."

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.760
But they were at TI, and that meant they had a chance.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:12.720
A chance to win, but perhaps more importantly, a chance to get revenge on their former captain,

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:14.760
their brother who betrayed them.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.360
"It is obviously never going to be easy to win a TI. Nobody has done it twice.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:26.120
But this year I think our chances are actually better than they've ever been.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.920
That's my personal gut feeling."

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:30.800
OG  had a tough group, arguably the harder of

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:36.520
the two, but they stayed strong, even after taking a 2-0 loss to Fly and EG

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:37.600
on the second day.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:44.480
(Casting)

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:49.600
And in the end, they came out in fourth, with a spot in the upper bracket and a clear path

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.340
to a fated rematch against EG.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:58.720
Both EG and OG dispatched their first round opponents with ease, 2-0.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:40.580
(Casting)

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:45.600
They were qualified for the upper bracket semi finals for a match against each other.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:47.360
The stage was set.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.420
EG against OG.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:51.040
Blue against Green.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:53.160
Brother against brother.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:55.360
Fly against N0tail.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:24.400
"Everyone has their own analogy about this matchup. There's many stories to be told.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:29.400
But obviously one that dates back to the old OG squad. And how now these two squads

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:31.360
have come to be in their current form.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:35.660
Winter, do you think that's gonna play a role in this matchup between the two?"

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:40.300
"Yeah both teams understand each other really well in terms of drafting, what they want to do."

00:07:40.400 --> 00:08:24.400
(Casting)

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.760
Game 1 was close.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:44.080
(Casting)

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.360
And while game 2 looked close as well,

00:08:46.400 --> 00:09:14.620
(Casting)

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:17.740
EG still managed to snuff them out in a dominant

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:18.740
performance.

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:27.960
(Casting)

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.840
The  score was 1-1,

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:33.960
EG were still the favorite, and OG still the underdogs.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:39.020
Sitting directly across from Fly, N0tail knew what exactly how much was on the line.

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:42.400
He wasn’t just fighting for a spot in the upper bracket finals.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:45.080
He wasn’t just fighting for more prize money.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:47.940
He was fighting for his principles.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:54.420
For his belief in a team he and Fly built, on an understanding that loyalty and friendship

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:57.040
meant more than money or championships.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:00.580
N0tail was fighting for the very soul of OG.

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:03.100
And his team was behind him.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:05.600
Every step of the way.

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:09.220
Things got off to a bad start for OG.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:15.020
(Casting)

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:16.680
And they only got worse.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:33.660
(Casting)

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:39.500
(Casting)

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:42.380
EG had taken two Roshans, had pressure on

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:45.880
OG’s barracks and were getting ready to close out the game.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:49.320
But OG persevered, and pulled out a miracle.

00:10:49.320 --> 00:11:22.580
(Casting)

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:29.640
After a grueling, 53-minute game, OG emerged
victorious, and N0tail had his revenge.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:12:09.660
(Casting)

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:12.200
The time for revenge was over.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:15.580
Now it was time for vindication.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:21.420
"When it comes to OG, it's the element of surprise that they have to play on. So I'm expecting just a lot of

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.680
creativity from them.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:27.960
But if LGD show up with their absolute best, I do feel like they have an edge.

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:32.160
Yeah a lot of times it did feel like OG was kind of able to force mistakes out of their opponent,

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:36.380
by surprise. And then take advantage of that momentum, whereas LGD we discussed earlier

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:37.960
just plays a clean game.

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:41.780
Despite beating EG, OG had a long way to go.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:46.980
There was still one more team between them and the Grand Finals: PSG.LGD.

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:50.640
Up until 2018, TI was defined by a cycle.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:56.400
Every even year, a Chinese team lifted the Aegis, and LGD were the only Chinese team

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:57.940
left in the bracket.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:01.920
Of course, it wasn’t just fate that was on their side, it was skill.

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:07.170
LGD may have only come out of the group stage in third place, but they dominated two powerhouse

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:09.950
teams on their way to the upper bracket finals.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:15.080
2-0 over both Virtus.pro, And defending champions, Team Liquid.So when

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:27.980
(Casting)

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:30.700
But by now, OG were used to being the underdogs.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:34.640
This was already their best TI performance in the team’s history.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:37.100
Why not take it just a little farther?

00:13:37.100 --> 00:14:02.180
(Casting)

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:05.260
Once again, OG silenced their doubters.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:10.350
They defeated LGD 2-1 thanks to an incredible comeback, and secured a spot in

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:12.030
the Grand Finals.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:15.400
OG was one match away from the Aegis.

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:19.420
One match away from the victory that had escaped them for so long.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:25.120
One match away from proving that they didn’t need Fly or S4, they just needed to believe

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:29.260
in the thing that had gotten OG so far in the first place.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:33.400
The belief that working together as a team and trusting each other would get them the

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:34.640
rest of the way.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:41.880
LGD dispatched EG 2-0 in the lower bracket finals to earn another shot at OG,

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:45.200
OG took the first game,

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:57.040
(Casting)

00:14:57.400 --> 00:15:00.620
But LGD rallied, taking two one-sided games

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:02.120
back-to-back.

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:12.500
(Casting)

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:14.880
OG had their backs to the wall.

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:36.360
(Casting)

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:42.060
With so much on the line, with so little room for error, no one expected former coach Ceb

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.420
to save OG.

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:45.180
But, he did.

00:15:45.180 --> 00:16:01.200
(Casting)

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:04.800
And it kept them alive for one last game.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:10.360
OG went in with a lineup of some of the least-picked heroes at the tournament, and LGD took advantage

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:12.800
of that as soon as the game started.

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:24.080
(Casting)

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:29.640
Once again, LGD took an early lead, but OG had been here before.

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:34.160
The whole tournament was one big comeback, so what better way to close it out than with

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:35.520
one more.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:17:59.640
(Casting)

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:04.160
OG emerged victorious after a close, 3-2 series.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:07.800
Ater a tournament filled with comebacks and close calls.

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:11.360
After getting revenge on Evil Geniuses.

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:14.660
"A team that was shaken up months before this event."

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.620
"They just reformed the team."

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:22.000
"Topson, he's only been playing for a couple of days,  and now he's won TI."

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:26.340
"Oh my goodness. OG."

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:30.080
"Congratulations to OG, they deserved it."

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:34.560
"They played out of their minds this entire tournament, they didn't follow anyone else's strategy

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:36.860
maybe that was the stepping stone."

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:39.280
"They just played their own game, and it was miraculous."

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:43.680
But perhaps most importantly, they emerged victorious after proving themselves.

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:47.600
"Cinderella story ain't got nothing on this."

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:54.880
"OG! Your TI8 champions!"

00:18:55.600 --> 00:19:03.020
At The International 2018, N0tail, JerAx, Ceb, Ana and Topson proved that the fundamental

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:05.900
belief that created OG was true.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:11.540
Sometimes, sticking together, working hard and believing in the team you’ve built means

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:15.560
more than the best all-star roster that money can buy.

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:19.260
Even when your friends lose their way and become your enemy,

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.760
Even when the world is against you,

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:25.320
"I would not have picked them as a favorite for a single series they played at TI."

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:28.440
You persevere, because the trust you’ve

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:30.580
created can win anything.

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:33.760
"That's what it's for. That right there. "

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:36.620
"You're a TI Champion n0tail."

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:40.340
"I guess. It's real. It's f***ing real."

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:42.620
"Breathe it in, take your time."

